sile material for six to seven warheads per year. North Korea is the tenth country to develop and most recent to openly test nuclear weapons. North Korea is also believed to have one of the world's largest chemical weapons stockpiles. North Korea is party to the Biological Weapons Convention, one of four United Nations members not to ratify the Chemical Weapons Convention, and the only country to announce withdrawal from the Non-Proliferation Treaty (NPT).","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/North_Korea_and_weapons_of_mass_destruction","source":"Wikipedia","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"places":[{"title":"North Korea","extract":"North Korea, officially the Democratic People's Republic of Korea (DPRK), is a country in East Asia. It constitutes the northern half of the Korean Peninsula and borders China and Russia to the north at the Yalu (Amnok) and Tumen rivers, and South Korea to the south at the Korean Demilitarized Zone (DMZ). The country's western border is formed by the Yellow Sea, while its eastern border is defined by the Sea of Japan. Pyongyang is the capital and largest city.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/North_Korea","source":"Wikipedia","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","iso2":"KP"}],"arc":{"reports":56,"first_seen":"2026-10-12T02:37:19Z","first_title":"North Korea continues streak of weapons tests with multiple ballistic missile launches","first_url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMifEFVX3lxTFBPaGVTQ2poU192cFhMYzRnWjRJS2N4Y2dPUTVySjJsTVM3V2tIYzJzRy1iX0ExT0tMbTdNdFVXNEY5RGR1aUQzNUs3MWpPc2g0Tmg3VVBhWUQ1MDhfbHJ2cWQ1MGx0VW1zVmt5Z0pzVzByTjZBbC1FUlIwVlQ?oc=5","first_publisher":"CBS News","earlier":[{"id":"e_3b732097f4b4","title":"North Korea tests attack drones as Kim calls for 'absolute superiority'","date":"2026-10-30T00:22:55Z","url":"https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261030-north-korea-tests-attack-drones-as-kim-calls-for-absolute-superiority","publisher":"© KCNA, via Reuters","verification":"single_source_report"},{"id":"e_008065a6417f","t